<<~ ahu slot=`#/purpose`>>

!! The controller's handoff ~ one seat, passed in the open

A session that holds the CONTROLLER's seat drives the build toward the roadmap's attractor (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-attractor`>>): it briefs lanes, routes their handbacks, pushes green heads, keeps canon and the changelog true, and brings the operator only what changes authority, custody at rest or identity bytes. This carrier holds what a session needs to take that seat: the practice, the state, and the way two live sessions pass the seat while both stand.

Read with it, in order: the boot seed (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot`>>), the roadmap's cold start (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/cold-start`>>), then #/the-lane-law.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-seat`>>

!! The seat ~ what the controller does

* ''It briefs lanes.'' One lane per feature path, each led by one lead whose lineage the brief names (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-seats`, `#/the-tiers`), its crew standing as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names. A lead's brief stands as a file, and the lead writes a resume sheet beside it.
* ''It keeps up to five lane slots filled'' (the sixth worktree holds the train). At every resume it reads `ListAgents` against the road: a lead whose seat vanished relaunches from its resume sheet and brief, and a slot that frees fills from the roadmap's order. The controller lands a one-line CI cure itself at most; a second cure means the lane's lead relaunches. A brief stays short and points at the shared law; it names the lane's ground, the ground it leaves alone, its first line of handback, and where it stops.
* ''It routes handbacks'' and owns one watcher per seat. A handback answers with one status line and plain notes. A finding on another lane's ground travels to that lane as a message or a patch.
* ''It lands batches.'' A lane pushes its own branch once per feature. The controller reads the lane's CI and held-out on the head (`node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha> --branch <branch>`: the full CI workflow, the container drivers of `held-out.yml`, and the shards where a bisect ran; it answers GREEN, RED or UNREADABLE, `--wait` reads until neither workflow stands unread), runs one train over the batch with `node tools/land-train.mjs` (`--plan` prints the commits and pushes nothing), and pushes the span while no run flies (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`). A red reading routes to the lane whose ground it touches; an UNREADABLE reading waits and reads again, and counts as neither green nor red.
* ''It keeps the record.'' Changelog bullets for what a person can do, written after reading `git diff HEAD -- CHANGELOG.md` clean; road commits ride behind a batch. Canon true-ups by a read-only collision of the roadmap against the tree, then hand-applied high-confidence lines.
* ''It settles forks down the ladder'' `working-procedures#/forks` names, and takes a house reading, marks it as one, and builds. A parked item stays parked; a turn ends on an act taken.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-practice`>>

!! The practice ~ what every lane keeps

* ''A refused command stops the lane.'' Never retry it, reshape it, split it, switch tools for it, or hand it to another spirit. The lane reports it; the controller surfaces it to the operator. A sidestep that reaches the same end counts as a retry.
* ''Edits happen in the lane's own worktree,'' committed there on the lane branch with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>` after `git status --short` and `git diff HEAD -- <path>` show only the lane's lines. One write per command line. No inline script writes into the main tree. A lane worktree leaves by a plain `git worktree remove` after its census; one that initialized submodules refuses a plain remove, so the lane proves its files landed and asks the operator for the `--force`. A train worktree leaves by its land script, which proves its final tree equals the pushed span tree first.
* ''Never `git stash`'' in any form, `git stash list` included; never `--no-verify`; never a foreground `sleep`, alone or chained: a long run goes in the foreground with a long timeout, or in the background with its completion notice.
* ''Red first, with a control''; a race gets pinned by the product's own event, never by a sleep, a retry loop or load. A load probe lives only as an opt-in triage script under `tools/`.
* ''The plugin bundle and genesis move only by the controller's word.'' A lane that changes `packages/lararium-tw5/` source or tiddlers rebuilds the bundle in the same commit and declares the gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; one labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` folds every declared row.
* ''Scratch roots alone'' for founding, standing or unlocking (`tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs`, then `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs`); never the operator's homes; never a real passphrase, domain or credential.
* ''After a machine restart'' the session scratchpad empties and every worktree under it vanishes. Durable state lives in git and in the session folder; a resumed lane re-reads its resume sheet, provisions a fresh worktree at HEAD, and rebuilds.
* ''O-takiage'' closes every lane and every settle as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-otakiage` names it.
* ''Fetch before you act, and again before you push.'' Another lane can merge into the work branch between two turns; a lane that pushes past it, or reasons from a stale origin, cures the wrong tree.
* ''A local green proves the tree it read.'' A worktree whose `node_modules` link into another checkout tests that checkout's build; every vitest config refuses a stale or foreign `dist` (`tools/vitest-dist-guard.mjs`). Provision lane worktrees with `tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>`, and run the heavy battery through the battery lock (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-battery`).
* ''One red in CI masks every package after it.'' `pnpm test` runs the packages in order and stops at the first red, so a cured red can reveal the next. Before pushing a cure, run the packages that come after it, or read the next CI run whole.
* ''Read the containers' own logs before naming a cause.'' A held-out cell uploads each container's log as an artifact (`gh run download <run> -n <cell>`); tallying each container's own lines split the carriage red where the witness's verdict could not. An in-process reproduction holds one Repo, so it cannot show a defect that lives between a CLI process and a running daemon.
* ''Give a sandboxed spirit the logs it cannot fetch.'' A Codex build or read seat reaches no network; fetch the failing job logs and hand it the excerpt as a file.
* ''A review lands nothing until a second face reads it'' (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lens-law`): a cheap eye's clean read clears nothing, and a tensioned finding gets measured by running it.
* ''Launch background spirits through the harness's background mode'', never a plain `&`: a plain `&` brings no completion notice, and `pgrep -f <pattern>` matches its own shell's command line.
* ''Shell traps in zsh'': `$R:t` reads as a path modifier, so write `${R}:path`; an unquoted variable holding several paths does not split (use `${(f)VAR}`); a `grep` pattern starting with `<<^` treats the caret as an anchor (use `grep -F`); `rm` on a path built from variables trips the safety check, so remove by literal path.
* ''A corrupt object heals by the operator's hand.'' `git fsck --full` names it; rebuild that pack in a scratch repo from an intact working copy and verify it there (run inside the damaged repo, `verify-pack`'s collision check reads the corrupt copy); the swap into `.git/objects` stays the operator's act.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lane-law`>>

!! The lane law ~ what every lead's brief points at, so a session on any machine reads it here

A session reads this carrier and the roadmap alone; no note outside the repository binds a lane. A lead's brief stays short, names its ground, the ground it leaves alone and where it stops, and points here.

!!! The crew
* ''The crew's seats, shapes and launches'' stand at `mixed-model-swarm`: which lineage holds which seat (#/the-seats), the local and cloud crews (#/the-shapes), the lens law, the Copilot seat's read-only role and budget, and the Codex and Copilot launch lines (#/the-launch).
* A lane hands back ONCE, short, in the shape `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names: one `<<~ status "…">>` line, the head, the CI and held-out readings, the story and its walk, rulings taken from canon with sources, true operator asks.

!!! Git
* A git command that writes runs alone on its line. Never `git stash` in any form, `git stash list` included (a PreToolUse hook, `tools/stash-guard.mjs`, refuses any Bash call that reaches it, and `.codex/rules/stash.rules` forbids its prefix to Codex); never `--no-verify`; never touch `.git/config`; never push the span (`feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`) or `main`, since a lane pushes its own lane branch; never `git worktree remove --force` on a lane worktree, since only the land script force-removes the train worktree it made.
* A lead works in its own worktree (`node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>` provisions one: inputs copied, every package built and stamped, no link left pointing into the main tree), and checks `git config core.bare` reads `false` before and after.
* A lead commits on its lane branch in its own worktree after `pnpm build`: it confirms the built CLI answers, reads `git status --porcelain -- <paths>` and `git diff -- <paths>` showing only its lines, then commits with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`. It never commits or reverts a line another hand wrote. A subject reads `lar:///ha.ka.ba/<pkg-or-bag>/<area>/<w1.w2.w3> — plain summary`; `-F`, never `-m`.

!!! Refusals and waiting
* A refused or denied command stops that step. Never retry it, reshape it, split it, switch tools for it or hand it to another spirit; save the work as a patch and hand back at once. The controller surfaces it to the operator.
* No foreground `sleep`, alone or chained. A long run goes in the foreground with a long timeout, or in the background with its completion notice.

!!! The battery
* One battery per batch, run through the battery lock as `mixed-model-swarm#/the-battery` orders it; one e2e file runs locally and the whole sets ride the lane branch's CI. A red CI run gets bisected (`node tools/burst-bisect.mjs <lane> <good> <bad>` or `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>`), never guessed. A live commit says so in its message and ends a batch only where later work builds on its bytes.
* Suites run from source under a scratch `HOME` and a scratch `LAR_ROOT`, with `LAR_BAGS` unset. Never `pnpm install` in the main tree. Before landing a test file, the charter and gate-dial funnels and the unbuilt-laws witness run.
* No standing test code produces load; a race gets pinned by a handshake between the parties.

!!! Canon and genesis
* Each commit carries its canon lines; law lives in one carrier and the roadmap points at it. Prose keeps L-Prime and stays evergreen. A carrier re-stamps with `lares meme normalize <file>`, one file per call, never piped. Identity keys in a first fence never change. Never edit `bags/elyncia*`, `ftls`, `sdm`, `wtf`, the boot seed, or the submission-guarded carriers.
* A change that moves a plugin bundle rebuilds and commits the bundle and declares the gap in `genesis/unbaked.json`; only a labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` folds it, on the controller's word. A step that would move bytes a genesis artifact carries stops and reports which bytes move.
* Custody, vault and sealed writes count as destroy-class: scratch roots alone, synthetic names and keys only, never the operator's homes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-cloud-lanes`>>

!! The cloud lanes ~ the briefs a cloud session takes by name

A cloud session opens on branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, stands the house from the boot seed, reads the roadmap's #/the-attractor, #/cold-start and #/rulings, this carrier whole (#/the-lane-law binds it), `working-procedures`, and its lane's kit, then walks its lane below. It leads as the Episkopos over the cloud crew `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes` names.

A cloud lane commits on its OWN branch, `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--<lane>`, cut from `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`, and pushes that branch alone, once per feature (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-feature-unit`); CI and held-out fire on it, and the lane reads them with `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha> --branch <branch>` (through the GitHub connector where the container's `gh` holds no login). The committed `.claude/settings.json` runs `tools/stash-guard.mjs` before every Bash call; a refusal from it stops that step. It never pushes `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` or `main`: the controller lands each lane branch in a batch (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`). It merges `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` into its lane branch once, right before its push, where a conflict asks. Its hand-back lists the canon and changelog lines for the roadmap and `CHANGELOG.md`, and the lane edits neither. It stops at a clean boundary when context runs short and hands back in the lane law's shape, with its lane branch and head.

!!! Lane `wire-socket` ~ past lane
Train W's assembled cutover landed as PR #44: every vessel socket opens through the sealed face gate on one handshake, fleet join serves every face, a fresh browser device stands at the floor, and a herm answers the knock where a Nexus carries it. The roadmap's `W` rows name what stays owed.

!!! Lane `carriage-fold` ~ a local session's lane
Kit: <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/carriage-fold-lane`>>. Roadmap row `W18`: the carrier folds walk the roll anchors (PR #50, merged 2026-10-19), and `P20`'s gate half reads a place contract across a roll (PR #54), so held-out reads green on every driver; DreamDom-Wright builds `F6` on lane `holder-owner`, owing the deliberate cross-epoch held-out cell beside it. A lane under `mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`: its own sub-branch, the work swarm's build pair in one worktree, the other lineage's read, the overwatch, a pull request.

!!! Lane `browser-custody` ~ past lane
Its custody API landed (the roadmap's `B1` row names what it built and what stays owed). Its boot caller rides with whichever lane next holds `open-browser-vessel.ts` and the web boot. The persona roots' seal waits built and red-first on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--persona-root-seal`: the root mint refuses `no-custody-slot`, so it merges only after that boot binds a slot and unlocks before `openBrowserVessel`.

!!! Lane `kahu-plane` ~ past lane
Train P after N landed: the chartered classes, exact-bytes promotion, Kahu-cabal admission, the co-signed steward map, the re-anchoring fence and the anchored ancestry count, with R-KAHU witnessed across two vessels. The crossroads crossing asks the seats (`P21` built). The roadmap's `P18` to `P20` name what stays owed. `P18` rides with whichever lane holds both vessel composers. `P19` and `P20` wait half-built on `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--gate-ancestry`, its commit message naming the writer and verifier cure that lands them.

!!! Lane `scout` ~ past report
The dated `next-path-scout.md` report records the earlier tree; its top line names the commits that supersede its stale observations.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/state`>>

!! State ~ the controller trues this section at every handoff

The span carries, through PR #137 (tonight, 2026-10-31): the agent's intent plane (`I1`) and its relay seat (`I2`, PRs #112 and #125), the floor's trust chain (`W14` to `W16`), the bounded refold (`G15`), the porch's bundles one, two, three, five and six, the record port (D2), the bonds that keep every seed below the floor (`K15`), the hands spine through its fourth slice, `K19` whole (PRs #110, #118, #121 and #127: one provider per joined face, the content fence denying by default, content unable to claim the channel, a session acting only as the face it wears, and a realm feed bound through the face→leaf bond), D3's mirror (PRs #111, #117 and #123: full-glass DreamDOM through the port grant, booting stock TW5 over a re-baked genesis), the staged-only e2e vectors reading SKIPPED, never green (PR #113), the cold-boot rest (PR #119), the passkey keyslot (PR #124), CI's Test job run as cells (PR #120), the founding walk (PR #128: a person founds, seeds and joins, and the leaf mounts the hearth's canon from the Kahu realm), the Codex seat launcher and the battery lock (`tools/launch-codex.mjs`, `tools/battery.sh`, PR #129), and the three-state verdict with the land train (`tools/ci-verdict.mjs`, `tools/land-train.mjs`, PR #130). Landed since PR #130: #131 `K20`, #132 `I3`, #133 `P26`, #134 `W27` and #137 porch bundle five, plus the tool commits (the land train carries a green head; `launch-codex` reads floor 0%). About to land: #135 `rcx` and #136 `ralias`. Building: `testlever`. Next: the keystone's six feature units, `U1` the signer hand-over into the island, then `U2` to `U6`, from the road's `O1` and sealed-store rows. The working contract lives in canon `mixed-model-swarm` (`testlever` carries tonight's lines there). The road's open rows sit in their strides; each train's state reads in `stable-founding-road#/the-trains`.

* ''The crew'': `mixed-model-swarm#/the-seats` holds the seats, `#/the-tiers` the placement, `#/the-seat-law` the Codex seat law. Spend reads from the tools' own logs through the controller's `spend.py`, which binds no lane. A Codex seat launches through `tools/launch-codex.mjs` (`--dry-run` shows its walls) and a heavy battery through `tools/battery.sh`; the controller's own scripts stand until a seat launches clean through the tools.
* ''Lanes in flight'' (under `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/`), in the order a clean start launches them:
** Wave one, three lanes on disjoint ground. Founding: the Kahu canon's integrity (`P26`: a member's synced change counts only under Kahu reach, the steward's succession across a leaf reissue and a paper restore, a whole-record conflict verb), in `d3-glass/wt`. `K19`: a face row's answer rides the socket alone (`K20`), in `k19b/wt` (`k19b/brief-socket-answers-next.md`). Relay: the intent plane under re-pin, re-target and growth (`I3`), in its own worktree (`i2-owed/intent-plane-plan.md`).
** Wave two. `K19`: per-face content-key seats and mints (`K21`, `k19b/brief-seats-next.md`). Founding: the lazy library mount, `W5` and `W7`, and the contract walk (`FW`; the lazy-mount patch stands at `d3-glass/lazy-mount/`).
** Wave three. The mirror and custody arc, `M2` to `D4` (the side lane of the road, `fable/brief-mirror-next.md`), and porch bundle four: `G6` outside the vessel files, `/cas` verifying a body before the index names it, and the load flakes (`G46`).
* ''After the three waves'': D3's remaining width work and the reference-phone measures; the hands room's other lanes (the profile-verb gate, the watcher's lease, the fleet view, `F10`, `F11`); the bake's critical path (`W26`'s fifth slice, the browser ceremony that seats a place card, `G37`, `X0`'s readiness).
* ''Ruled since the rest call'' (operator, 2026-10-27 to 2026-10-29): old shapes and shape gates burn now; the land chain caps the Docker build cache at 15GB; a session binds one (face, anchor), identity read as a relation for places as for faces; each joined face holds its own provider; full-glass DreamDOM runs a main-thread TW5 mirror opened by the port grant, never a URL flag, painting skinny first and promoting to full, one mirror step then teardown, the mirror the visible surface; a browser on a node's box takes a port, one setup of many, and a user's cap-stack holds an anon device-browser vessel or a fleet of them, no node infrastructure; a person's lighter choice carries an experience, never a width; Copilot Fusion stays deferred until after the founding (the crew keeps its own workflows, inversion of control); the sensorium rests until the fully founded Lararium proof.
* ''Recurring faults to watch'': a CI load sometimes reds `wiki-shore-*`, `filter-cts`, `uds-session-switch` or `vessel-reboot` tests that pass alone; PR #114 cured the store race and the shore waits, so a recurrence after it reads as a new fault, never a rerun. The local train installs when a lane moves the lockfile. Under a loaded box, the custody census's staged unlock, the mesh scale ratio, the `shore-writes` TW5 dropdown case and a git author email leaking from the environment read red and pass alone (`G46`); an unreachable GitHub reads as UNREADABLE, never red.
* ''Rulings the crew still asks of the operator'': the mirror's engine in an iframe realm; DreamDOM's key grain, its interaction goldens family and its `core` charter (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`).
* ''Disk law'': worktrees under `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/`, a provision reads `df` first and stops under 60G free on C:, a land removes its worktree.
* ''Shared ground'': lanes meet on the two vessel composers; one lane at a time holds a composer hunk, and the others hand theirs to the controller.
* ''The parked branches'', each read before any merge: `--w26-own-canon`, `--browser-bag-ledger`, `--instruments`, `--symbol-anchor-truth`, `--gate-ancestry`. `--projection-loom` (PR #84) moves under its own seat; the crew leaves it alone.
* ''The Copilot allowance'': 300 premium requests a month, resetting on the first; a read seat costs a handful, a PR review about 13. The run log's `Requests N Premium` line states spend; the entitlement cache reads last-known.
* ''The sensorium rests'' until the fully founded Lararium proof (operator ruling, 2026-10-27): no lane re-stands the sensorium or the mempalace sidecar before it, and CI runs no sensorium Python suite until that lane re-hooks it.
* ''The controller's train reads a tally, never an exit'': a suite log with no "Test Files" line reads red. A lane stays strict: red-first per commit, its own battery, its own CI and held-out green. The controller lands batches through the land tool (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`); a lane on an older base lands when the span moved only by lands since.
* ''The operator's own founding'': the persistent node vessel founds after the road's work and its aftermath land, by hand, on a TTY; no spirit founds it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-live-handoff`>>

!! The live handoff ~ two sessions, one seat, passed by word

A session can close and a fresh one boot from carriers; a ''live'' handoff lets both stand for a while, so the new seat can ask the old one what no carrier caught. The seat passes by explicit word, never by drift.

# ''One controller at a time.'' Only the seat-holder pushes the feature branch, fills lane slots and commits to `CHANGELOG.md` or the roadmap. The other session reads, asks, and works only lanes the seat-holder hands it by name.
# ''The outgoing seat trues #/state'' in this carrier, commits it, and names its lanes in flight: which will finish under it, and which pass to the incoming seat with their resume sheets.
# ''The incoming seat reads first'': the boot seed, the roadmap's cold start, and this carrier whole, #/the-lane-law included. Then it asks the outgoing seat, by session name over the message channel, whatever stays unclear: a lane's intent, a house reading's reason, a red that looked like a flake.
# ''The seat passes by message.'' The outgoing seat sends "the seat passes to <session>" once no push stands in flight and every lane it keeps has a named owner; the incoming seat answers "the seat holds". Until that answer, the outgoing seat still holds it.
# ''Lanes keep their spirit.'' A running lane answers the session that launched it. A lane that passes gets a new lead launched by the incoming seat from its resume sheet, never a message to a subagent of another session.
# ''Questions flow both ways after the pass''; the outgoing session may keep a lane to finish, and reports its handback to the new seat-holder as a lane would.

<<~/ahu>>

